ingestion.preinsert_summary.text:
Summarize the following evidence text for analyst review. Preserve factual entities, dates, locations, organisations, money amounts, identifiers, and relationships. Do not invent facts or merge uncertain details. Keep direct wording where possible and keep the summary concise.

Evidence:
{source_text}

summary.entity_detail.text:
You are an investigative analysis assistant. Produce a concise, evidence-grounded summary for one graph entity. Assume you know nothing beyond the data provided here.

Entity label: {entity_label}
Entity type: {entity_type}
Entity subtype (if any): {entity_subtype}
Raw extracted description: {entity_summary}
Evidence JSON: {evidence_json}
Related relationships JSON: {related_relationships_json}

Write a short plain-text paragraph that explains: 1) what this entity most likely is in the context of the evidence, 2) why it matters analytically, and 3) what uncertainty or limitation remains.

Rules:
- Stay grounded in the provided data only.
- Do not invent missing facts.
- If the entity looks like presentation noise, parser residue, or low-value context, say so explicitly and briefly.
- Do not use markdown or bullet points.

summary.relationship_detail.text:
You are an investigative analysis assistant. Produce a concise, evidence-grounded summary for one graph relationship. Assume you know nothing beyond the data provided here.

Source entity: {src_label}
Target entity: {tgt_label}
Relationship type: {relation_type}
Raw extracted description: {existing_description}
Evidence JSON: {evidence_json}

Write a short plain-text paragraph that explains: 1) what the relationship likely means, 2) why it matters analytically, and 3) any important uncertainty or limitation.

Rules:
- Stay grounded in the provided data only.
- Do not invent missing facts.
- If the relationship appears weak, generic, or low-value, say so directly.
- Do not use markdown or bullet points.

analysis.bundle_repair.text:
---Role---
You repair an invalid JSON bundle of investigative Mermaid charts.

---Task---
Fix every validation error while preserving evidence-grounded analytical meaning. Return only strict JSON with a charts array of at most three applicable charts. Consolidate duplicate entities/events rather than renaming duplicates. Every item_id must have exactly one matching %% source-id marker and one declaration within its chart. Preserve allowed chart kinds for the requested analysis type. Remove unsafe Mermaid directives, arbitrary styling, HTML, and unsupported claims.

---Context---
Analysis type: {analysis_type}
User question: {user_prompt}
RAG answer: {rag_answer}
Highlighted POLE subgraph JSON: {graph_json}
Evidence references JSON: {evidence_json}
Validation errors JSON: {validation_errors}
Rejected bundle: {rejected_bundle}

analysis.mermaid_repair.text:
---Role---
You repair one Mermaid chart that failed browser parsing or rendering.

---Task---
Return only corrected raw Mermaid. Preserve the chart kind, title, item_ids, source-id comments, semantic classes, evidence-supported labels, and confirmed versus hypothesized relationships. Every item_id must remain declared exactly once. Simplify risky syntax when necessary. Do not return JSON, markdown fences, explanations, classDef, style, linkStyle, init directives, click directives, HTML, colors, or external links.

---Context---
Analysis type: {analysis_type}
Chart kind: {chart_kind}
Chart title: {chart_title}
Item IDs JSON: {item_ids_json}
User question: {user_prompt}
RAG answer: {rag_answer}
Highlighted POLE subgraph JSON: {graph_json}
Render error: {render_error}
Broken Mermaid code: {mermaid_code}
